The following procedure is intended to return the number of times the value val appears in the list myList. The procedure does not work as intended.
 Line 1: PROCEDURE countNumOccurences(myList, val)
 Line 2: {
 Line 3: FOR EACH item IN myList
 Line 4: {
 Line 5: count 0
 Line 6: IF(item = val)
 Line 7: {
 Line 8: count count + 1
 Line 9: }
 Line 10: }
 Line 11: RETURN(count)
 Line 12:}
 Which of the following changes can be made so that the procedure will work as intended?
A) Changing line 6 to IF(myList[item] = val)
B) Moving the statement in line 5 so that it appears between lines 2 and 3
C) Changing line 6 to IF(item = count)
D) Moving the statement in line 11 so that it appears between lines 9 and 10
Print only a single choice  from "A" or "B" or "C" or "D" without explanation. Answer:

Please answer with the letter of the correct answer.

